3. How a Browser Requests and Displays a Web Page

When a user enters a website address in a browser:

User enters the URL.
Browser finds the server's IP address using DNS.
Browser sends an HTTP/HTTPS request to the server.
Web server receives the request.
Server sends files such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and images.
Browser receives these files.
Browser creates the webpage structure from HTML.
CSS is applied for styling.
JavaScript is executed when required.
Browser renders and displays the webpage.

